## Module 7: Credit Note Management

**Objective:** Track the financial value of medicine returns and identify discrepancies.

This is the most important differentiating feature of PharmaReturn.

### Features

- Upload credit-note documents.
- Enter credit-note number.
- Enter supplier details.
- Enter credit amount.
- Link credit notes to return requests.
- Record credit-note date.
- Track pending credits.
- Support partial credits.
- Identify amount discrepancies.

### Example

| Description | Amount |
|---|---:|
| Expected credit | ₹80,000 |
| Supplier-approved amount | ₹65,000 |
| Actual credit note | ₹58,000 |
| Unreconciled difference | ₹7,000 |

The system should flag the ₹7,000 difference for investigation.

### Reconciliation Statuses

- Not credited.
- Partially credited.
- Fully credited.
- Credit discrepancy.
- Under review.
- Reconciled.

### User Story

As an accountant, I want to compare expected return credits with actual supplier credit notes so that I can identify missing or incorrect credits.

### Acceptance Criteria

- Credit notes can be uploaded and recorded.
- Credit notes can be associated with return requests.
- The system calculates the difference automatically.
- Partial credits are supported.
- Users can mark discrepancies as resolved.
- Adjustments and reconciliation changes are logged.

