# 11. Regulatory and Operational Considerations

PharmaReturn must be designed as a documentation and workflow management product.

It should not:
- Automatically approve medicine returns.
- Promise that a supplier will accept a return.
- Treat all manufacturers' return policies as identical.
- Automatically authorise expired medicine redistribution.
- Replace applicable statutory records or accounting processes without validation.

The product should support configurable return workflows and retain evidence of the decisions made by the distributor and supplier.

Before commercial deployment, obtain appropriate Indian pharmaceutical regulatory and GST/accounting advice. Return and credit-note handling must follow applicable requirements, including relevant CDSCO guidance and GST rules.

