# 13. MVP Acceptance Criteria

The MVP is considered ready when a pilot distributor can:

1. Register and create a business account.
2. Add suppliers and configure their return policies.
3. Import medicine batch inventory.
4. Identify batches that may qualify for returns.
5. Understand why a batch is eligible or ineligible.
6. Create a return request for multiple batches.
7. Track the return request through its lifecycle.
8. Upload a supplier credit note.
9. Compare expected and actual credit values.
10. Identify pending or short credits.
11. View total recovery and pending financial values.
12. Export a basic recovery report.

A successful end-to-end test must demonstrate this complete workflow using sample data and at least one real-world pilot workflow with customer permission.

